{
  "description": "The pinned benchmark corpus of the M5-0.4 census: the 23 repositories of Oasis's published evaluation (DegenerateUSER/Oasis), each pinned at its default-branch HEAD commit on 2026-09-17 together with the SHA-256 of the GitHub source archive at that commit. One census module per repository.",
  "provenance": {
    "source": "https://github.com/DegenerateUSER/Oasis",
    "what_oasis_publishes": "the 23 repository names in benchmarks/README.md and report_draft.md, and raw GitHub search output under evidence/ that resolves each name to its org/repo; Oasis publishes no commit identifiers, archive digests or module subdirectories",
    "pin_method": "each repository pinned at its default-branch HEAD commit on 2026-09-17; archive fetched from codeload.github.com at that commit and digested with SHA-256; the digest makes the pin drift-proof in both directions",
    "selection_method": "Oasis's repository list is published, so no independent candidate selection was made; the org/repo resolution of every one of the 23 names comes from Oasis's own published evidence/gh_search_candidates_raw.txt, and each resolution is unique and still public at the pin date. dpdesi/serverless-architecture-patterns pins its default branch feat/subsystem-composition; every other repository pins main."
  },
  "module_rule": "The census module within each repository is the test-equipped module directory nearest the archive root. Concretely, over every directory of the archive: a gradable pairing is a directory that carries at least one .tf file (the module subdirectory) together with a test root that is either that directory itself (root-colocated) or one flat subdirectory of it carrying at least one .tftest.hcl file. The pairing with the shallowest module subdirectory wins; ties break lexicographically by subdirectory, then test root. The rule is mechanical and reproducible from the archive alone; Oasis's own evaluation ran at repository level over every test-equipped module root, which is one axis on which the side-by-side comparison is limited, and the limitation is published with the census.",
  "test_root_semantics": "root means the suite is colocated with the module subdirectory; any other value is the flat subdirectory of the module subdirectory that carries the suite, passed to the engine as its TestDirectory.",
  "json_stratum": "json_declared records whether the module subdirectory carries root .tf.json declarations. At the 2026-09-17 pin no module in the corpus carries any, and no repository in it carries any .tf.json or .tftest.json file at all: the corpus's JSON stratum is empty, so the #82 census's JSON-declared denominator is zero over this corpus.",
